    "allocation": "a crossing endpoint pair is allocated to the current root, representing its unique lowest separating node",
    "capacity": "Nat.choose (k - 2) (rank - 1)",
    "claim_boundary": "The census is bounded evidence only; it neither proves the general frontier bound nor supplies a global injective charge.",
    "contexts": "every recursively deep-below coloring on every labeled support and every compatible nontrivial root split",
    "endpoint_projection_shortcut": "the left or right endpoint set would support the direct classical cup--cap reduction only if it avoids a color-rank+1 chain and an opposite-color-(k+1-rank) chain",
    "endpoint_transition_hall": "for each retained span and each endpoint, encode the past and future predecessor/successor rank incidences as lower ideals of the truncated (rank-1)-by-(k-rank-1) Pascal grid; the span may use any ideal between meet and join at either endpoint, and the tested claim is that all spans admit distinct representatives from those two interval unions",
    "frontier": "fixed-color fixed-exact-rank intervals containing no distinct candidate interval",
    "rank": "maximum local monochromatic cup/cap chain size with the exact ordered endpoint pair; terminal strong-k contexts are skipped"
  },
